#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:2
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:4
msgid ""
"Each entry below describes something that has actually happened, and how "
"it presents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:8
msgid "OCR or extraction stops making progress"
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:10
msgid ""
"**Symptom** — the progress window sits still, or the log fills with ``502"
" upstream: All connection attempts failed`` and ``500 EngineCore "
"encountered an issue``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:14
msgid ""
"**Cause** — the 502 is a symptom, not the fault: the front proxy is "
"answering, but the model worker behind it died and is restarting. The 500"
" is that worker on its way out. Repeating in a cycle means it is crash-"
"looping, usually out of GPU memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:19
msgid ""
"**What the app does** — brief outages are absorbed by a short retry. A "
"sustained one pauses the batch, polls the server, and resumes "
"automatically when it comes back, keeping the queue intact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:23
msgid ""
"**What to check** — the server's own log for the actual crash (out of "
"memory, a CUDA fault). Running OCR and the language model on the same GPU"
" makes this more likely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:28
msgid "A paper comes back \"PARTIAL\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:30
msgid ""
"Part of the bibliography was parsed and the rest was not. The parsed "
"entries are saved; the paper stays unchecked so a later run replaces "
"them. Nothing is lost, and re-running is safe — references are written "
"per source, replacing the previous set rather than accumulating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:35
msgid "The progress line names the reason:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:37
msgid "``bad JSON``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:38
msgid ""
"The model's answer was cut off. The batch is retried with a larger "
"budget, then split, before being given up on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:41
msgid "``no array``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:42
msgid ""
"The model answered in prose rather than data — usually because the text "
"it was handed is not a bibliography."
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:45
msgid "``timeout``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:46
msgid "No answer within the time limit. The batch is split and retried."
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:48
msgid ""
"Details, including the offending response, go to "
"``~/.papermeister/logs/biblio_YYYYMMDD.log``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:52
msgid "Zotero write-back fails with 403"
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:54
msgid ""
"The API key is read-only. Either issue a key with write permission on the"
" library, or turn write-back off in Settings → Zotero and keep changes "
"local."
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:58
msgid "Zotero rejects an update with 400"
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:60
msgid ""
"Usually a field that does not exist on that item type — for example a "
"journal name on a ``bookSection``. The app maps journal-like fields per "
"item type and will say which field was refused. For a standalone PDF with"
" no parent item, promote it to a real item first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:66
msgid "A PDF will not download"
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:68
msgid ""
"If the attachment record exists but the file is not in Zotero's storage, "
"the download returns 404 and the paper is marked failed. Check whether "
"the file opens in Zotero itself; if it only exists on your local disk, it"
" needs to be uploaded to Zotero first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:74
msgid "The frozen app fails to start on Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:76
msgid ""
"If you built it yourself: build in a clean virtual environment with conda"
" **off** the PATH. Building inside a conda shell mixes conda's Qt "
"libraries into the bundle, and the frozen app then dies with a missing-"
"procedure error. ``build_desktop_clean.bat`` does this correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:82
msgid "The database is damaged"
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:84
msgid ""
"Do not run scripts against the live database from WSL while the Windows "
"app is writing to it — the two disagree about file locking and can "
"desynchronise an index."
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:88
msgid ""
"Recovery is usually cheap, because index damage does not lose rows: copy "
"the database somewhere local, ``REINDEX`` the affected index, and confirm"
" with ``PRAGMA integrity_check``. Take a backup with ``VACUUM INTO`` "
"before any bulk operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:94
msgid "Search finds nothing for a word I can see"
msgstr ""

#: ../../troubleshooting.rst:96
msgid ""
"Check the **Text** tab: if the page is blank there, OCR did not capture "
"it and the paper needs reprocessing. Search reads the stored text, not "
"the PDF."
msgstr ""

